      "date": "Oct 27",
      "source": "High Plains Journal",
      "summary": "Sen. Jerry Moran expects no farm bill action before the election; a lame-duck push is possible, or it slips to the new Congress in January. He notes the 2026 safety net is already set by the 2025 reconciliation law and urged producers to use ARC/PLC, which USDA projects at about $13.8B for crop year 2025.",
      "tag": "Farm bill",
      "title": "Farm bill on hold until after the Nov. 3 election",
      "url": "https://hpj.com/2026/10/27/farm-bill-remains-in-holding-pattern-until-after-nov-3/"
    },
    {
      "date": "Oct 23",
      "source": "farmdoc Farm Policy News",
      "summary": "FIELDS grants back eight nitrogen, potash and sulfur projects across 16 states, with completion expected in 2027–28. USDA projects modest near-term price relief (roughly 4–5% on nitrogen and potash); no Montana plants are named.",
      "tag": "USDA programs",
      "title": "USDA awards $573M to expand U.S. fertilizer production",
      "url": "https://farmpolicynews.illinois.edu/2026/10/usda-to-provide-573m-to-boost-domestic-fertilizer-production/"
    },
    {
      "date": "Oct 21",
      "source": "farmdoc Farm Policy News",
      "summary": "Adding the $8B fuel relief to USDA's forecast puts government payments near a third of 2026 net farm income, topping 2020's record. Fuel aid may not pay out until late November or December, which matters for operating-line paydown timing.",
      "tag": "USDA payments",
      "title": "Diesel aid could push 2026 farm payments to a record $55 billion",
      "url": "https://farmpolicynews.illinois.edu/2026/10/diesel-aid-could-push-2026-government-payments-to-farmers-to-record-55-billion/"
    },
    {
      "date": "Oct 19",
      "source": "USDA",
      "summary": "One-time 2026 payments run by FSA, based on planted acres, ERS cost-of-production and WASDE yields and prices; crop insurance not required. Per-crop rates for Title I commodities come in November, and no sign-up window is set yet. Producers should set up a Login.gov account linked to USDA ahead of time.",
      "tag": "USDA payments",
      "title": "USDA announces $8 billion Harvest Fuel Relief program",
      "url": "https://www.usda.gov/about-usda/news/press-releases/2026/10/19/trump-administration-announces-8-billion-harvest-fuel-relief-program"
    },
    {
      "date": "Oct 16",
      "source": "USDA Farm Service Agency",
      "summary": "2025 PLC triggered on 17 Montana crops including wheat, barley, canola, lentils and dry peas ($160,000 limit, 5.7% sequestration), plus 2026 CRP rent on about 928,000 acres. 2026 ARC/PLC sign-up closes Dec. 11; 2027 sign-up opens Nov. 2.",
      "tag": "USDA payments",
      "title": "About $303 million in ARC/PLC and CRP payments heading to Montana",
      "url": "https://www.fsa.usda.gov/news-events/news/10-16-2026/usda-boosts-montana-agricultural-economy-303-million-safety-net"
    },
    {
      "date": "Oct 9",
      "source": "Holland & Knight",
      "summary": "The House passed its bill in April and Senate Ag reported S. 5526 on Sept. 24; SNAP cost-sharing is the main sticking point. Government funding runs out Dec. 11, the same day as the 2026 ARC/PLC deadline.",
      "tag": "Farm bill",
      "title": "Farm bill is a realistic year-end goal, with another extension as fallback",
      "url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2026/10/beyond-the-midterms-congress-faces-converging-year-end-deadlines"
    }
